next
  Summary: Adaptive target lead

  Effectiveness
    Reaction
      - Added Target Lead: NPCs now lead a moving target by the round's actual flight time, computed live from range and the weapon's bullet speed, instead of a fixed amount.
        Rank sets how true the lead is: top ranks lead on the mark and hit movers while low ranks over-lead and overshoot, but the error is now bounded and scales with range instead of the old fixed overshoot at every distance.

1.1.5
  Summary: Counterflank, Reaction, Commitment, player-only maneuvers, no dead windows, danger from your setup, performance, fixes

  Combat
    Maneuvers
      - Added Counterflank: a stalker firing at a distant target wheels around when you close to contact range instead of giving you his back.
      - Added per-weapon-kind fire: pistol and rifle bursts, single sniper shots, in place of the uniform 5-round burst.
      - Changed targeting: maneuvers now weigh range, angle, line of sight, and cover, run only in fights you are in, and drop those that would change nothing.
      - Changed retreat and flee: retreats reach real cover behind the stalker, cornered stalkers hold their ground, and cowardly factions flee before they fight.
    Commitment
      - Added Commitment: stalkers see a fight through instead of twitchy strafing and cover-hopping.
        A stalker keeps his fire, presses a flank, or finishes a reload rather than dropping a good action for a marginally better one, breaking off only when it stops making sense.
        Needs a recent engine build.

  Effectiveness
    Accuracy
      - Added Moving Fire, a per-rank curve: fire on the move scales by rank, so low ranks spray while repositioning and top ranks stay steady.
    Danger
      - Changed detection to read from your installed config instead of overriding its tuning.
      - Fixed enemy gunfire to alert stalkers even when not aimed at them.
      - Fixed scripted danger carrying over to a reused id on respawn.
      - Fixed a corpse-investigation crash when its reaction fired before its stage was set.
    Reaction
      - Added Tracking Speed, a per-rank curve for how tightly the barrel follows a moving target.
      - Added Vision Speed, a per-rank curve for detection speed at range.
      Both are set per stalker at spawn and need a recent engine build.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Fixed the master toggle only applying after a game restart.
    Jamming
      - Fixed it to stay inert on engines without the misfire hook instead of failing when disabled.
    Ammo
      - Fixed armor-piercing rounds reverting on the wrong weapon after a mid-fight switch.

  Performance
    - Changed all combat, healing, and ammo monitoring to run on scheduled passes instead of per-frame callbacks. The whole mod now costs 3 timer compares per frame, whatever the NPC count.
    - Fixed a rare freeze of every timed system on mid-maneuver deaths.

  Development
    Ballistics
      - Added a toggleable recorder of shot outcomes near you, off by default and free while off.
        It logs per-rank hit rates split by shooter motion, damage dealt, burst lengths per weapon, and per-bullet aim error including lead over/undershoot against a moving target.
    Debug HUD
      - Changed the HUD to headline the active maneuver in green for the takeover's whole life, with wider name columns and a twice-per-second refresh.

1.1.1
  Summary: startup fix

  Fixed
    - An outdated xlibs no longer crashes AlifeTactics on load. The dependency check now shows the
      "update xlibs" message instead of a raw script error from the MCM platform footer.

1.1.0
  Summary: Maneuvers, Crossfire, Danger, Disclosure, Ammo, Jamming, Healing, AOEngine, platform status

  Combat
    - Maneuvers: an intermittent combat takeover that borrows a stalker for a committed maneuver.
      Stalkers kite when crowded, hold sniper aim when stalled, take cover then flee when badly hurt.
      Borrowed stalkers hold fire when they have no clear shot instead of firing into cover.
      Companions are excluded by default. Replaces the old Stance Switch system.

  Effectiveness
    - Crossfire: a same-faction friendly-fire damage block, default on.
      Same-faction hits deal no damage, tunable back up to full vanilla.
    - Danger: an xr_danger rework, always-on bug fixes plus 3 toggleable improvements.
      Hits, ricochets, and gunshots read separate config rows, with weather-scaled detection range.
      Sniped or shot-at NPCs react at any range, even to gunfire vanilla left unanswered.
      Corpse investigation survives despawned corpses, drives the right stalker, takes its cover.
    - Disclosure: a new survivor gate, default on.
      An outright kill no longer discloses the shooter, so stealth kills stay quiet.
    - Fixed lone NPCs never being alerted to their shooter (disclosure was squad-only).

  Mechanics
    - Ammo: NPC armor-piercing ammo drawn from the boxes NPCs carry, default on.
      Veteran-rank and higher NPCs fire AP with real ballistics until their carried supply runs out.
      Each engagement rolls a rank- and fire-rate-weighted chance to burn a carried AP box.
    - Jamming: NPC weapon-jam suppression that stops the demonized per-rank jam-and-reload loop.
      Actor jams stay vanilla. Default on, needs demonized 2026.6.1+.
    - Healing: limping now matches the NPC's weapon and clears after HP recovers or in combat.
      Healing NPCs no longer freeze in place or ignore enemies that appear mid-gesture.

  MCM
    - Renamed the Disclosure, Crossfire, and Healing internals to match their page names.
      Saved settings on those 3 pages reset to defaults on update (the reset warning covers it).

  Compatibility
    - AOEngine v0.55+ support.
    - Added dynamic checking of xlibs and xray-monolith/AOEngine versions with a compatibility verdict.
    - The Danger rework is a runtime patch, so it coexists with GAMMA AI Rework and REDONE.
    - Ammo goes inert while the engine cvar g_ai_unlimited_ammo is 0, so NPC ammo is not drained twice.

1.0.0
  Summary: First release, hit sharing, NPC self-healing fix, per-rank accuracy, long-range rifle crouch
  First release. Four independent systems on top of one internal core. Full MCM configuration.
  Added: Hit Sharing - on first faction-enemy hit, force-disclose shooter to every online squadmate (force_set_goodwill, enable_memory_object, register_in_combat). Distant patrols and suppressor victims now engage on hit 1. Disclosure decays after the configured retention (default 2 game minutes of no further hits from that shooter), then re-fires on the next hit. New squad members inherit existing disclosures on spawn. Previously-offline shooters coming back online replay disclosure to every member of the squads tracking them.
  Added: NPC Self-Healing - DLTX overlay restores vanilla medkit and bandage item lists in xr_eat_medkit. Heal rate multiplier, per-rank healing-charge probability (novice, experienced, veteran, master), limping overlay, heal animation.
  Added: Accuracy - per-shot, per-rank NPC dispersion curve replacing the engine's broken rank curve. 8 per-tier dispersion sliders (novice 1.00 to legend 0.38).
  Added: Stance Switch - long-range rifle carriers (DMRs, battle rifles, bolt-actions: SVD, Mosin, SVT40, SKS, M82 and the rest of the kind=w_sniper LTX class) crouch when engine selects LookOut or HoldPosition. Crouch carries forward into KillEnemy, WaitInCover, HoldAmbushLocation through body_state inheritance.
  Added: MCM reset-to-defaults button (Development tab).
  Added: console test commands at_spawn, at_spawn_veteran, at_spawn_master, at_spawn_far, at_dump.
